      "problem": "Let\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ p \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ p\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $v\\cdot w=3$, find the value of $p.$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting from the equation $v\\cdot w=3,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $p$ and then solve for $p$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot w & =3 \\\\ -2\\cdot 2+p\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot p & =3 \\\\ -4-4p+15+6-3p & =3 \\\\ -7p+17 & =3 \\\\ 7p & =14 \\\\ p & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $p=2.$",
